<Base title="Experience building U.S. businesses" description="The operating experience behind ARONIA: building Vincit USA from its first customer to eight-figure revenue, and co-founding and growing Privv.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Experience</div><span class="eyebrow">The experience behind ARONIA</span><h1>From first U.S. customer<br/><span class="serif copper">to eight-figure revenue.</span></h1><p class="lead">The lessons behind ARONIA come from building businesses, earning customer trust, and changing direction when the market challenges your assumptions.</p><p class="experience-note">These are examples from Ville Houttu’s operating roles at Vincit USA and Privv. They describe the founder experience behind ARONIA.</p></div></section>
<section class="section story" id="vincit"><div class="wrap"><div class="story-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">01 / Vincit USA</span><h2>From the first customer<br/>to eight-figure U.S. revenue.</h2></div><span class="small-label">Building the U.S. business</span></div><div class="story-columns"><div><p>In 2016, I moved to California to build the U.S. business for Vincit, a publicly traded European software and design company. We had a strong European track record, but no U.S. customers, local reputation, or established go-to-market motion.</p><h3>Earn the first reason to believe.</h3><p>I landed our first customer, Logitech, then built the local positioning, credibility, team, and go-to-market. We won category-leading customers and completed three acquisitions to accelerate growth.</p><p>Revenue doubled each of the first four years, reaching eight figures within five years. The business grew to a team of more than 60 people and was named to the Inc. 5000 three consecutive years.</p><div class="number-line"><div><strong>8 figures</strong><span>U.S. revenue</span></div><div><strong>3×</strong><span>Inc. 5000</span></div><div><strong>3</strong><span>Acquisitions</span></div></div><p class="quote">“Build credibility. Listen to the market. Invest behind what works.”</p></div><figure class="image-frame" style="margin:0"><img class="story-photo inc5000-photo" src="/assets/photography/ville-inc5000-v2.jpg" alt="Ville Houttu at an Inc. 5000 event" width="1050" height="1400" loading="lazy"/><figcaption class="image-credit">2021 Inc. 5000</figcaption></figure></div><div class="credibility-strip" style="margin-top:45px"><span class="small-label">Selected clients during Ville’s journey</span><div class="logo-carousel"><div class="logo-row carousel-track">{[['logitech','Logitech'],['yamaha','Yamaha'],['splunk','Splunk'],['nytimes','The New York Times'],['uag','UAG']].map(([f,a])=><img src={`/assets/logos/clients/${f}-charcoal.png`} alt={a} width="300" height="100" loading="lazy"/>)}</div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section sand story" id="privv"><div class="wrap"><div class="story-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">02 / Privv</span><h2>From an idea<br/>to $1M ARR.</h2></div><span class="small-label">Finding a repeatable sales motion</span></div><div class="story-columns"><figure class="image-frame" style="margin:0"><img class="story-photo privv-presentation" src="/assets/photography/ville-privv-presentation.jpg" alt="Ville Houttu presenting Privv in a meeting room" width="1200" height="1600" loading="lazy"/><figcaption class="image-credit">2025 Privv presentation</figcaption></figure><div><p>I co-founded Privv and built a SaaS project management platform for capital projects, helping building owners and owner’s representatives manage budgets, schedules, cash flow, and workflows.</p><h3>Change the assumptions when the market does.</h3><p>We identified the initial market, learned where the ICP was not working, and pivoted to a stronger segment. We built a repeatable sales motion around that focus.</p><p>That sales engine took Privv from zero to $1M ARR, with more than $4 billion in projects managed through the platform.</p><div class="number-line"><div><strong>$1M</strong><span>ARR</span></div><div><strong>$4B+</strong><span>Projects managed</span></div><div><strong>SaaS</strong><span>Capital projects</span></div></div><p class="quote">“When the market challenged the original assumptions, we changed the assumptions.”</p></div></div></div></section><section class="section" id="in-the-market"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-intro"><span class="eyebrow">Out in the market</span><div><h2>Bring the business<br/><span class="serif">into the conversation.</span></h2><p class="muted">Presenting the product and sharing the experience behind it with industry and entrepreneurial audiences.</p></div></div><div class="market-photos"><figure><img src="/assets/photography/ville-aca-award-presentation.png" alt="Ville Houttu presenting on stage" width="1448" height="1086" loading="lazy"/><figcaption><strong>ACA Innovation Award winner</strong></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/assets/photography/ville-venture-cafe-v2.jpg" alt="Ville Houttu speaking on a panel with an AZ Inno Start-Ups to Watch backdrop" width="1200" height="1600" loading="lazy"/><figcaption><strong>AZInno Startups to Watch 2025</strong></figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="wrap section-intro" style="margin-bottom:0"><span class="eyebrow">What carries forward</span><div><h2>Evidence before investment.<br/>Focus before scale.</h2><p class="lead">Every business is different. The operating discipline carries across: choose a clear starting point, get close to buyers, and use what you learn to decide the next move.</p><a class="text-link" href="/foundation-sprint/">How ARONIA puts that into practice <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section><CTA/></Base>
